      "reading": "てきせつ",
      "reason": "「適切」 (tekisetsu) is a な-adjective that is the most common and general Japanese equivalent for 'appropriate', 'suitable', or 'proper'. It aligns well semantically and grammatically with the English lemma for general learning purposes."
